 "result": "**Where to look**\n\n- `src/tessel/app.py:1175-1190`, the `else` branch of `Tessel.link_for`. With no active request, it uses the app context's `url_adapter` if there is one. Otherwise it calls `self.build_url_binder(None)`. If that returns `None`, it raises your `RuntimeError`.\n- `src/tessel/app.py:550-558`, `build_url_binder`. With `request=None` it returns an adapter only when `config[\"SERVER_NAME\"]` is not `None`. The default is `None` (`app.py:215`), so a background job with no request gets no adapter and hits the error.\n\n**Fix**\n\nSet `SERVER_NAME` so Tessel knows which host to build external URLs for. Set the other two as needed:\n\n```python\napp.config.update(\n    SERVER_NAME=\"example.com\",       # required\n    APPLICATION_ROOT=\"/\",            # path prefix, if the app is mounted under one\n    PREFERRED_URL_SCHEME=\"https\",    # defaults to \"http\"\n)\n```\n\nOutside a request, `link_for` then returns external URLs (`_external` defaults to `True`). Call it inside `with app.app_context():` or via `app.link_for(...)` directly. `docs/config.rst:279-286` documents this requirement.",
